. * nwrem tutorial 1: a first relational event model on a phone-call log
. * Requires the core nwcommands and the package nwrem.
. * Run from this folder; the data are in ../data (events and actor attributes).
. 
. nwrem version
nwrem version 1.0.7, 26oct2026
  core package nwcommands : installed (development copy, no distribution date)
  native plugin           : none (Mata only)
  compared with           : R relevent 1.2-1
  license                 : GNU GPL-3

. 
. * --- the event data: one row per call, with the time it happened ---
. import delimited "../data/calls_events.csv", clear
(encoding automatically selected: ISO-8859-1)
(3 vars, 439 obs)

. list in 1/5

     +--------------------------------+
     | sender   receiver    eventtime |
     |--------------------------------|
  1. |     72         50   1220733470 |
  2. |     43         51   1221102974 |
  3. |     43         51   1221784293 |
  4. |     43         22   1221785882 |
  5. |     43         55   1221787264 |
     +--------------------------------+

. count
  439

. display "span in days: " (eventtime[_N] - eventtime[1]) / 86400
span in days: 42.125949

. 
. * --- declare the events as an event network ---
. * The log mentions 54 of the 84 students; the other 30 never call or are called.
. * They still are possible senders and receivers, so we add them as isolates.
. levelsof sender, local(a) clean
1 2 5 7 8 11 16 20 21 23 24 27 29 30 31 32 36 37 42 43 44 46 47 51 55 58 62 64 66 67 68 70 71 72

. levelsof receiver, local(b) clean
1 3 4 6 8 9 11 12 14 16 20 21 22 23 24 25 27 30 31 32 33 34 35 36 42 43 44 45 46 50 51 54 55 58 60 61 63 64 66 67 68 70 
> 71 74 76 77

. local all : list a | b

. local miss

. forvalues i = 1/84 {
  2.     if !`: list i in all' local miss `miss',`i'
  3. }

. local miss = substr("`miss'", 2, .)

. nwset sender receiver, directed eventtime(eventtime) name(calls)

. nwaddnodes calls, nodenames(`miss')

. nwset
(1 networks)
--------------------
      calls

. 
. * --- a model of activity: do busy senders and popular receivers keep their roles? ---
. nwrem calls, nodsnd nidrec
------------------------------------------------------------
Relational event model (ordinal partial likelihood, MLE)
Network: calls                         Actors: 84
Events: 439                            Log likelihood: -3.12e+03
------------------------------------------------------------
------------------------------------------------------------
       calls | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
      nodsnd |   10.57478   .3530761    29.95   0.000     9.882761    11.26679
      nidrec |   11.32606   .3391393    33.40   0.000     10.66136    11.99077
------------------------------------------------------------

. 
. * --- a model of history: do people call those they called, or who called them? ---
. nwrem calls, frpsndsnd frrecsnd
------------------------------------------------------------
Relational event model (ordinal partial likelihood, MLE)
Network: calls                         Actors: 84
Events: 439                            Log likelihood: -2.27e+03
------------------------------------------------------------
------------------------------------------------------------
       calls | Coefficient  Std. err.      z    P>|z|     [95% conf. interval]
-------------+----------------------------------------------------------------
   frpsndsnd |   6.254331   .1453025    43.04   0.000     5.969544    6.539119
    frrecsnd |   2.034655   .1400245    14.53   0.000     1.760212    2.309098
------------------------------------------------------------

. display "events: " e(N) ", actors: " e(nodes) ", log likelihood: " %9.2f e(ll)
events: 439, actors: 84, log likelihood:  -2274.05

. display "effect of inertia on the odds: x" %6.1f exp(_b[frpsndsnd] * 0.1) " per 10 percentage points"
effect of inertia on the odds: x   1.9 per 10 percentage points

. 
